      "message": "The change itself looks right and minimal to me.\n\nCould the commit message say what goes wrong without it, though? As far as I can see, both mappings still work as 16KB VMAs in a 4KB process: the kuser helpers are copied just below `0xffff1000` (`vdso.c:197`), and `get_unmapped_area()` returns a 16KB-aligned address for the sigpage (`p3s_adjust_unmapped_area_info()`), so the sigreturn code copied to the start of the page (`vdso.c:216`) is where `context.sigpage` points.\n\nIf the goal is the 4KB `[vectors]` and `[sigpage]` layout that AArch32 code sees on a 4KB kernel, I\u0027m not sure do we need to support it?",
